From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:52:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: msm: take warm restarts through PS_HOLD

The secure firmware on SDM845 devices such as the comma four implements
PSCI 1.1 without SYSTEM_RESET2 (PSCI_FEATURES returns NOT_SUPPORTED), and
its SYSTEM_RESET is a cold reset. So there is no firmware call for a warm
reset: RAM does not survive a reboot or a panic, and with it go the console
and crash logs that ramoops keeps in pstore. reboot=warm makes no
difference. The downstream kernel avoided this with qcom,force-warm-reboot,
which selects the PMIC's warm reset and drops PS_HOLD itself.

For boards whose DT says qcom,no-firmware-warm-reset, register a restart
handler ahead of the firmware (PSCI) one that drops PS_HOLD when
reboot_mode is warm. pm8941-pwrkey selects the PMIC's reset type for
PS_HOLD from reboot_mode at restart time, before this handler runs.
Without the property nothing changes, and firmware that implements a warm
reset keeps getting PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2.

While at it, check the return values of the handler registrations.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
index c7eb6dc8e9..a2b78a32ac 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/pm.h>
 
 static void __iomem *msm_ps_hold;
+static bool msm_no_fw_warm_reset;
 
 static int do_msm_poweroff(struct sys_off_data *data)
 {
@@ -23,20 +24,46 @@ static int do_msm_poweroff(struct sys_off_data *data)
 	return NOTIFY_DONE;
 }
 
+static int do_msm_firmware_restart(struct sys_off_data *data)
+{
+	/*
+	 * For firmware without a warm reset (no PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2, and a cold
+	 * SYSTEM_RESET), take warm restarts through PS_HOLD, which keeps RAM.
+	 * The PMIC is set up to warm reset when PS_HOLD drops.
+	 */
+	if (msm_no_fw_warm_reset && reboot_mode == REBOOT_WARM)
+		return do_msm_poweroff(data);
+
+	return NOTIFY_DONE;
+}
+
 static int msm_restart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
+	int ret;
+
 	msm_ps_hold = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(msm_ps_hold))
 		return PTR_ERR(msm_ps_hold);
 
-	devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
-				      128, do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
+	msm_no_fw_warm_reset = of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node,
+						     "qcom,no-firmware-warm-reset");
+
+	ret = devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
+					    SYS_OFF_PRIO_FIRMWARE - 1,
+					    do_msm_firmware_restart, NULL);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
+				     "failed to register firmware restart handler\n");
 
-	devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_POWER_OFF,
-				      SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT, do_msm_poweroff,
-				      NULL);
+	ret = devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_RESTART,
+					    128, do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
-	return 0;
+	return devm_register_sys_off_handler(&pdev->dev,
+					     SYS_OFF_MODE_POWER_OFF,
+					     SYS_OFF_PRIO_DEFAULT,
+					     do_msm_poweroff, NULL);
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id of_msm_restart_match[] = {
